WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.424
<v Instructor>So now let's talk about</v>

2
00:00:01.424 --> 00:00:03.770
AWS Cost Allocation Tags.

3
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.510
So we know we can tag resources

4
00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:08.350
and the reason we do so is that so we can compare

5
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.640
which one relate to one another.

6
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.210
But we can also use these tags

7
00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.930
for cost allocation, first endpoint.

8
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.690
So using cost allocation tags,

9
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.310
we can enable detailed costing reports.

10
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.620
They're just like tags,

11
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.980
but now when we look at billing reports,

12
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.740
they will show up as additional columns,

13
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.800
which will allow us to divide our data more specifically.

14
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.870
There are two types of cost allocation tags.

15
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:34.890
The first one is AWS Generated Cost Allocation Tags,

16
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:38.010
which is automatically applied to a resource you create

17
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.670
and it starts with the prefix, AWS.

18
00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.830
For example, AWS created by.

19
00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.140
They're not applied to resources created

20
00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.820
before the activation of these tags.

21
00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.380
Now you also have user tags.

22
00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.130
Those are the tags that you create, you, your user,

23
00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.610
and they start with the prefix, user.

24
00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:59.160
Now cost allocation tags just appear in the billing console,

25
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.280
not anywhere else,

26
00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.500
and it takes about 24 hours for the tags to show up

27
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.430
in the reports.

28
00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.100
So it is important for you as a solution architect

29
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.210
to have a tagging strategy in your AWS accounts,

30
00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.380
in cross accounts,

31
00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.290
so that when you look at your billing reports,

32
00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:15.430
you can group all the data by the tags that you need.

33
00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:16.740
And that's it, very simple,

34
00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.230
but it's all you need to know for the exam.

35
00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:19.980
I will see you in the next lecture.

